1
00:00:39,973 --> 00:00:40,807
Haruka.

2
00:00:40,940 --> 00:00:41,775
Yeah?

3
00:00:41,908 --> 00:00:42,909
Let's go home.

4
00:00:49,182 --> 00:00:50,116
Metzen.

5
00:00:58,491 --> 00:01:02,562
The son of Chairman Uchikanda...

6
00:01:09,002 --> 00:01:10,136
Does it hurt again?

7
00:01:10,570 --> 00:01:12,272
No. I'm fine.

8
00:01:13,506 --> 00:01:15,075
Too much practice?

9
00:01:17,510 --> 00:01:18,578
Mom...

10
00:01:19,512 --> 00:01:24,784
I'm going to win the audition and
become a principal dancer.

11
00:01:25,685 --> 00:01:27,854
Okay. So keep practicing.

12
00:01:28,421 --> 00:01:31,291
Dr. Daimon, wait.

13
00:01:31,758 --> 00:01:33,193
Did you forget?

14
00:01:33,293 --> 00:01:37,897
You said you'd help me pick out
some clothes and gifts for Mai.

15
00:01:37,964 --> 00:01:40,166
Oh... I don't feel like it.

16
00:01:41,000 --> 00:01:42,202
I'll treat you to Korean BBQ.

17
00:01:42,569 --> 00:01:43,436
Really?

18
00:01:43,503 --> 00:01:44,370
Let's go.

19
00:01:46,573 --> 00:01:47,407
Haruka?

20
00:01:50,543 --> 00:01:51,511
Mai's mom.

21
00:01:52,645 --> 00:01:53,880
Let's go.

22
00:01:53,947 --> 00:01:56,749
Dr. Daimon, this is Haruka Kokonoe.

23
00:01:56,816 --> 00:01:58,651
Mai's friend from ballet school.

24
00:02:01,054 --> 00:02:03,923
I'm friends with her mom.
She's also divorced.

25
00:02:05,091 --> 00:02:06,159
What's up?

26
00:02:09,496 --> 00:02:11,631
Ms. Jonouchi, Mom's friend.

27
00:02:11,998 --> 00:02:12,999
Hello.

28
00:02:13,600 --> 00:02:15,568
Your grandfather?

29
00:02:16,202 --> 00:02:17,804
- Yes.
- Nice to meet you.

30
00:02:18,338 --> 00:02:20,073
She was visiting me

31
00:02:21,374 --> 00:02:22,809
and said her foot hurt.

32
00:02:22,876 --> 00:02:23,776
Oh...

33
00:02:25,044 --> 00:02:28,781
You have a ballet audition,
don't you?

34
00:02:29,716 --> 00:02:32,185
You should get it
properly examined.

35
00:02:32,552 --> 00:02:35,522
Where's the after-hours reception?

36
00:02:36,523 --> 00:02:37,423
I'll show you.

37
00:02:40,660 --> 00:02:42,629
What about Korean BBQ?

38
00:02:43,296 --> 00:02:44,164
Huh?

39
00:02:54,741 --> 00:02:58,211
<i>This is the story of</i>
<i>a lone wolf woman doctor.</i>

40
00:03:01,781 --> 00:03:07,353
Your son, Dr. Nishiyama,
is showing great promise.

41
00:03:08,354 --> 00:03:12,725
He's making his mark as a fine surgeon.

42
00:03:14,427 --> 00:03:15,361
But...

43
00:03:16,029 --> 00:03:20,567
there's one thing that worries me.

44
00:03:22,535 --> 00:03:26,105
His devotion to Michiko Daimon.

45
00:03:26,539 --> 00:03:27,840
If you know what I mean...

46
00:03:29,242 --> 00:03:30,210
I...

47
00:03:30,376 --> 00:03:33,313
don't care about your power or you.

48
00:03:33,446 --> 00:03:34,514
I'm not interested.

49
00:03:36,849 --> 00:03:41,621
Chairman, you don't seem to
have an appetite.

50
00:03:42,922 --> 00:03:43,756
Please.

51
00:03:43,990 --> 00:03:45,325
Thank you.

52
00:03:46,326 --> 00:03:47,527
<i>In 2017</i>

53
00:03:48,228 --> 00:03:53,266
<i>the university medical system</i>
<i>regained its once-lost authority</i>

54
00:03:53,733 --> 00:03:59,639
<i>and the system on which lives depend</i>
<i>strayed away from what it should be.</i>

55
00:04:01,507 --> 00:04:06,212
In the midst of this, doctors free
from any establishment emerged.

56
00:04:06,546 --> 00:04:10,583
<i>Freelance doctors, in other words,</i>
<i>lone wolf doctors.</i>

57
00:04:13,152 --> 00:04:14,821
<i>This woman, for example.</i>

58
00:04:15,822 --> 00:04:19,826
<i>Despising the herd mentality, authority</i>
<i>and institutional restraints...</i>

59
00:04:20,393 --> 00:04:25,598
<i>Her solo weapons are her license</i>
<i>and the skills she has acquired.</i>

60
00:04:26,299 --> 00:04:27,600
Michiko Daimon.

61
00:04:28,735 --> 00:04:30,837
She must be destroyed quickly.

62
00:04:30,970 --> 00:04:33,273
Yes. I'm working on it.

63
00:04:33,406 --> 00:04:37,644
Also that locum doctor agency
that protects her.

64
00:04:40,346 --> 00:04:43,216
Even the locum doctor agency?

65
00:04:43,650 --> 00:04:45,852
If you can't do it, I will.

66
00:04:47,787 --> 00:04:51,624
That might not be so easy...

67
00:04:53,026 --> 00:04:54,661
There's no time.

68
00:05:02,402 --> 00:05:04,671
<i>Surgeon Michiko Daimon.</i>

69
00:05:05,171 --> 00:05:06,172
<i>Also known as...</i>

70
00:05:06,706 --> 00:05:08,374
<i>Doctor-X.</i>

71
00:05:38,571 --> 00:05:40,973
What were the test results
for that girl?

72
00:05:41,507 --> 00:05:43,376
Accessory navicular syndrome.

73
00:05:43,509 --> 00:05:45,211
Accessory navicular syndrome?

74
00:05:45,278 --> 00:05:48,915
Inflammation of an extra bone.
She just has to rest her foot.

75
00:05:49,048 --> 00:05:53,052
Accessory navicular syndrome.
It reminds me of Spain.

76
00:05:53,119 --> 00:05:53,953
Spain?

77
00:05:54,153 --> 00:05:56,389
Rafael Lopez, the pro tennis player.

78
00:05:56,456 --> 00:05:58,591
That good-looking guy?

79
00:05:58,791 --> 00:06:03,129
He was first diagnosed with
accessory navicular syndrome.

80
00:06:03,596 --> 00:06:06,199
- However...
- It was a navicular fracture.

81
00:06:06,399 --> 00:06:07,467
Fracture?

82
00:06:07,600 --> 00:06:11,170
If it's not treated,
it could lead to osteoarthritis.

83
00:06:12,105 --> 00:06:13,506
It's common in athletes.

84
00:06:13,773 --> 00:06:15,308
Does she play any sports?

85
00:06:15,408 --> 00:06:16,542
She's a ballet dancer.

86
00:06:17,276 --> 00:06:18,745
She should be re-examined.

87
00:06:18,811 --> 00:06:20,313
HISAKO KOKONOE

88
00:06:20,446 --> 00:06:22,348
Hey, Hiromi...

89
00:06:23,282 --> 00:06:25,718
You have one too many.

90
00:06:25,952 --> 00:06:27,487
You're right.

91
00:06:27,553 --> 00:06:29,989
That's "tahai."

92
00:06:31,524 --> 00:06:32,558
See?

93
00:06:32,625 --> 00:06:35,228
Violation!

94
00:06:35,294 --> 00:06:38,464
A penalty of 4,000 points
to each of us.

95
00:06:40,233 --> 00:06:41,634
That was Mai's mom.

96
00:06:42,435 --> 00:06:44,270
She suggests a re-examination.

97
00:06:47,106 --> 00:06:48,708
Why didn't you tell me?

98
00:06:49,041 --> 00:06:50,743
That you went to the hospital today.

99
00:06:52,211 --> 00:06:53,813
She said Grandpa took you there.

100
00:06:55,882 --> 00:06:58,151
I told you, didn't I?

101
00:06:58,751 --> 00:07:00,820
To keep your distance with him.

102
00:07:02,955 --> 00:07:04,724
Even if he's your father?

103
00:07:07,326 --> 00:07:08,728
That man...

104
00:07:12,765 --> 00:07:15,935
He's a failure as a father
and a human being.

105
00:07:20,273 --> 00:07:22,942
After a thorough re-examination

106
00:07:23,409 --> 00:07:26,612
we now know it's not
accessory navicular syndrome.

107
00:07:27,079 --> 00:07:30,049
- It's a navicular fracture.
- What?

108
00:07:31,184 --> 00:07:32,084
A fracture?

109
00:07:33,152 --> 00:07:35,688
It's not going to heal naturally?

110
00:07:35,822 --> 00:07:37,290
Was it a misdiagnosis?

111
00:07:38,491 --> 00:07:39,525
Ms. Kokonoe...

112
00:07:40,293 --> 00:07:42,662
A navicular fracture is often

113
00:07:42,728 --> 00:07:46,165
caused by spraining an ankle
or playing sports.

114
00:07:46,766 --> 00:07:50,937
The fracture is difficult to identify.

115
00:07:51,204 --> 00:07:52,038
Look.

116
00:07:52,672 --> 00:07:54,974
Stop making excuses.

117
00:07:57,009 --> 00:07:58,811
Please treat her right away.

118
00:07:59,779 --> 00:08:01,814
The fracture takes time to heal.

119
00:08:01,948 --> 00:08:03,683
She has a ballet audition.

120
00:08:03,983 --> 00:08:05,751
It has to heal.

121
00:08:05,885 --> 00:08:07,353
Then she needs surgery.

122
00:08:08,020 --> 00:08:09,021
Surgery?

123
00:08:10,790 --> 00:08:12,925
What kind of surgery?

124
00:08:12,992 --> 00:08:17,263
A metal screw will be inserted
to secure the fractured bone.

125
00:08:22,568 --> 00:08:23,636
You draw.

126
00:08:24,036 --> 00:08:25,538
Why me?

127
00:08:33,412 --> 00:08:34,447
Like this.

128
00:08:35,615 --> 00:08:38,851
You're going to insert
a metal screw in her foot?

129
00:08:39,252 --> 00:08:43,155
When the bone heals, the screw
will be removed in another surgery.

130
00:08:44,457 --> 00:08:46,592
She needs two surgeries?

131
00:08:46,759 --> 00:08:50,229
A protrusion of the screw might
affect her ballet performance.

132
00:08:50,296 --> 00:08:52,565
She's young.
It's better to remove it.

133
00:08:54,467 --> 00:08:57,136
How long will the treatment take?

134
00:08:59,338 --> 00:09:01,541
Four weeks for the bone to heal.

135
00:09:01,841 --> 00:09:04,744
Eight weeks to walk without crutches.

136
00:09:04,977 --> 00:09:07,947
With the surgery to remove the screw...

137
00:09:08,281 --> 00:09:10,149
For full recovery, I'd say

138
00:09:11,284 --> 00:09:12,285
half a year.

139
00:09:12,518 --> 00:09:14,253
She'll miss the audition.

140
00:09:14,654 --> 00:09:16,489
Isn't there a faster method?

141
00:09:16,622 --> 00:09:19,625
Not if she wants to keep dancing.

142
00:09:21,494 --> 00:09:23,095
Hey! Don't run!

143
00:09:23,162 --> 00:09:24,830
Haruka...

144
00:09:26,432 --> 00:09:30,703
Dr. Daimon, you should choose
your words more carefully.

145
00:09:31,404 --> 00:09:33,306
She's still a child.

146
00:09:34,774 --> 00:09:35,675
Also...

147
00:09:36,242 --> 00:09:38,978
if you're going to meddle,
make your own drawing.

148
00:09:39,478 --> 00:09:40,880
I'm not good at drawing.

149
00:09:43,282 --> 00:09:44,884
Let's go to another hospital.

150
00:09:46,752 --> 00:09:50,256
Maybe there's a doctor who
can heal you quicker.

151
00:09:56,596 --> 00:09:57,463
Here.

152
00:09:58,230 --> 00:09:59,765
That's a cool ballerina.

153
00:09:59,966 --> 00:10:01,400
Did you buy it?

154
00:10:03,603 --> 00:10:05,671
Someone made it for me.

155
00:10:08,874 --> 00:10:10,042
It's well made.

156
00:10:11,744 --> 00:10:14,714
Mom, I'll take the audition
without treatment.

157
00:10:15,348 --> 00:10:16,315
Haruka...

158
00:10:16,449 --> 00:10:18,751
I can put up with the pain.

159
00:10:23,689 --> 00:10:25,024
Attention, please.

160
00:10:25,091 --> 00:10:27,960
It's time for the year-end party.

161
00:10:28,094 --> 00:10:31,097
If you want to attend,
fill this out and turn it in.

162
00:10:31,831 --> 00:10:33,299
Year-end party?

163
00:10:33,633 --> 00:10:34,467
Are you going?

164
00:10:34,900 --> 00:10:35,735
Yeah.

165
00:10:36,102 --> 00:10:38,671
Who has time for
something like this?

166
00:10:38,804 --> 00:10:42,308
I hate it when people
get drunk and loud.

167
00:10:42,375 --> 00:10:44,477
Me too. The naggers.

168
00:10:44,543 --> 00:10:45,778
I'm not going.

169
00:10:46,078 --> 00:10:47,446
The organizer!

170
00:10:47,513 --> 00:10:48,781
Organizer?

171
00:10:48,848 --> 00:10:51,183
You're the organizer
again this year.

172
00:10:51,250 --> 00:10:52,585
But I did it last year.

173
00:10:53,185 --> 00:10:55,621
Organizer, Mamoru Hara.
Why me?

174
00:10:55,688 --> 00:10:57,023
I always think

175
00:10:57,289 --> 00:11:01,060
there's no other person
in this hospital who can

176
00:11:01,127 --> 00:11:03,229
organize a party better than you.

177
00:11:03,295 --> 00:11:04,797
- There is.
- There is not.

178
00:11:04,997 --> 00:11:06,132
Thanks.

179
00:11:09,335 --> 00:11:10,503
I don't believe this.

180
00:11:10,970 --> 00:11:12,605
Thank you.

181
00:11:12,738 --> 00:11:14,140
Thank you.

182
00:11:14,473 --> 00:11:16,709
Thank you. Bye.

183
00:11:20,279 --> 00:11:22,948
Haruka, go on home
without me.

184
00:11:23,916 --> 00:11:24,784
Okay.

185
00:11:31,924 --> 00:11:35,594
I withdrew Haruka from the audition.

186
00:11:37,296 --> 00:11:38,164
I see.

187
00:11:42,501 --> 00:11:44,003
I'm glad you're here.

188
00:11:45,838 --> 00:11:47,740
I wanted to talk to you.

189
00:11:53,312 --> 00:11:57,550
You're making Haruka
visit you a lot.

190
00:11:58,050 --> 00:11:58,918
Stop it.

191
00:11:59,952 --> 00:12:01,687
I'm not making her...

192
00:12:03,456 --> 00:12:05,858
I just wanted to tell you that.

193
00:12:06,258 --> 00:12:08,928
Is Haruka's foot that bad?

194
00:12:12,998 --> 00:12:13,933
You must be happy.

195
00:12:15,301 --> 00:12:18,738
Haruka will also have
to give up her dream.

196
00:12:20,806 --> 00:12:21,640
Hisako...

197
00:12:23,709 --> 00:12:26,011
You can't feed yourself
with the arts.

198
00:12:28,080 --> 00:12:29,448
Now you won't have to

199
00:12:30,916 --> 00:12:32,752
hit Haruka like you hit me.

200
00:12:34,487 --> 00:12:35,588
Back then...

201
00:12:42,328 --> 00:12:44,330
I feel so bad for Haruka.

202
00:12:45,731 --> 00:12:48,234
She's 13 already.

203
00:12:48,734 --> 00:12:52,605
Losing half a year at her age
is a big blow.

204
00:12:53,405 --> 00:12:55,374
Did you know?

205
00:12:56,275 --> 00:13:00,846
A ballet dancer can't become
a principal without recognition

206
00:13:00,980 --> 00:13:02,381
from an early age.

207
00:13:05,151 --> 00:13:06,485
Not interested, huh?

208
00:13:08,954 --> 00:13:10,389
Akira!

209
00:13:12,057 --> 00:13:16,462
About Rafael Lopez in Spain...

210
00:13:16,762 --> 00:13:17,830
You too?

211
00:13:18,097 --> 00:13:21,033
I was also thinking the same thing.

212
00:13:21,433 --> 00:13:23,002
What do you think?

213
00:13:23,736 --> 00:13:26,972
It wasn't possible in that
small town in Spain.

214
00:13:27,773 --> 00:13:29,141
I know...

215
00:13:31,277 --> 00:13:34,513
What are you talking about,
Dr. Daimon?

216
00:13:35,314 --> 00:13:36,415
Wait.

217
00:13:37,316 --> 00:13:38,450
For what?

218
00:13:38,517 --> 00:13:40,219
Just wait.

219
00:13:46,058 --> 00:13:48,327
The treatment schedule.

220
00:13:48,427 --> 00:13:49,562
Excuse me.

221
00:13:51,130 --> 00:13:53,499
You can recover in time
for the audition.

222
00:13:55,167 --> 00:13:57,269
What are you saying?

223
00:13:57,469 --> 00:13:59,038
We won't use a metal screw.

224
00:14:00,105 --> 00:14:02,074
And you'll only need
one surgery.

225
00:14:03,242 --> 00:14:04,143
Really?

226
00:14:06,278 --> 00:14:07,313
How?

227
00:14:09,915 --> 00:14:13,452
To secure the fracture,
instead of a metal screw

228
00:14:13,986 --> 00:14:17,389
we'll use one made of
the patient's bone.

229
00:14:17,656 --> 00:14:18,757
A screw made of bone?

230
00:14:19,658 --> 00:14:23,229
An osteosynthesis using
autogenous bone graft.

231
00:14:24,330 --> 00:14:27,700
The screw will integrate
into the bone

232
00:14:27,766 --> 00:14:31,103
so it won't affect
her ballet performance.

233
00:14:31,971 --> 00:14:35,774
No foreign body reaction.
No need to remove it later.

234
00:14:35,975 --> 00:14:38,978
On top of that,
zero cost for material.

235
00:14:40,646 --> 00:14:44,016
A screw from the patient's
bone... Is that possible?

236
00:14:44,650 --> 00:14:46,886
It makes sense.

237
00:14:47,486 --> 00:14:48,587
Seriously?

238
00:14:48,821 --> 00:14:51,824
From her ilium,
we'll cut out an almond...

239
00:14:52,825 --> 00:14:53,659
No.

240
00:14:54,393 --> 00:14:57,563
A peanut-sized bone fragment.

241
00:14:58,197 --> 00:14:59,231
Peanut?

242
00:15:00,332 --> 00:15:04,670
Then it'll be made into
a screw on the spot.

243
00:15:04,803 --> 00:15:05,804
On the spot?

244
00:15:06,005 --> 00:15:09,275
Process the bone during
the op in the OR?

245
00:15:09,508 --> 00:15:11,110
Then there's no need
for another op.

246
00:15:11,677 --> 00:15:14,179
The whole procedure should
only take about

247
00:15:15,180 --> 00:15:16,315
an hour and a half.

248
00:15:16,448 --> 00:15:17,516
Hold on.

249
00:15:18,684 --> 00:15:19,551
Yes?

250
00:15:20,753 --> 00:15:22,187
In the OR

251
00:15:23,255 --> 00:15:25,925
who will make the screw
and how?

252
00:15:26,625 --> 00:15:29,261
We, as doctors, don't have the skill.

253
00:15:31,463 --> 00:15:34,900
Daimon... You can do it?

254
00:15:35,834 --> 00:15:37,636
Of course I don't.

255
00:15:37,903 --> 00:15:38,771
There you go.

256
00:15:39,905 --> 00:15:41,206
So what are you going to do?

257
00:15:41,540 --> 00:15:43,742
The only ones with the skill are

258
00:15:43,809 --> 00:15:47,513
the engineering departments of
Keisei and Kanto Koga Universities

259
00:15:47,746 --> 00:15:51,183
and Mechanical Pro,
a precision equipment manufacturer.

260
00:15:53,419 --> 00:15:55,955
So the machine and the engineers

261
00:15:56,255 --> 00:15:59,725
are going to be in the OR
during the operation?

262
00:15:59,792 --> 00:16:01,460
- Yes.
- Have they agreed?

263
00:16:01,593 --> 00:16:02,428
Essentially yes.

264
00:16:03,262 --> 00:16:07,466
They've given us a positive feedback.

265
00:16:08,033 --> 00:16:12,705
They're happy to cooperate if
their precision processing technology

266
00:16:12,771 --> 00:16:14,340
helps to advance
Japanese medicine.

267
00:16:14,873 --> 00:16:18,744
I'll cut out a part of the patient's
bone with a micro saw

268
00:16:19,144 --> 00:16:21,714
and an engineer will
make it into a screw.

269
00:16:22,348 --> 00:16:25,651
Then I'll immediately secure
the fracture with it.

270
00:16:27,820 --> 00:16:29,888
What an incredible idea.

271
00:16:30,189 --> 00:16:31,056
Yeah.

272
00:16:32,157 --> 00:16:33,792
- Excuse me.
- What?

273
00:16:34,860 --> 00:16:37,663
May I assist you in this operation?

274
00:16:45,204 --> 00:16:46,271
Excuse me.

275
00:16:46,338 --> 00:16:50,376
The bone screw operation that
Daimon will be performing...

276
00:16:50,943 --> 00:16:53,379
Dr. Nishiyama volunteered
to assist her.

277
00:16:54,146 --> 00:16:56,415
Have you taken care
of the other matter?

278
00:16:56,515 --> 00:16:59,918
Yes. I've made the calls
as you instructed.

279
00:17:00,586 --> 00:17:01,420
Good.

280
00:17:03,622 --> 00:17:04,456
Thank you.

281
00:17:08,260 --> 00:17:13,499
Now Michiko Daimon and
Kanbara Locum Doctor Agency

282
00:17:14,466 --> 00:17:15,968
are finished.

283
00:17:21,540 --> 00:17:22,441
One more thing.

284
00:17:23,742 --> 00:17:25,010
This came for you.

285
00:17:27,846 --> 00:17:29,848
Thank you.
You may go now.

286
00:17:29,982 --> 00:17:30,949
Yes, Chairman.

287
00:17:42,828 --> 00:17:44,296
TEST RESULTS

288
00:17:44,430 --> 00:17:46,765
KAGENOBU UCHIKANDA

289
00:18:08,520 --> 00:18:09,922
Hello.

290
00:18:10,556 --> 00:18:11,757
Dr. Daimon.

291
00:18:12,858 --> 00:18:17,863
I appreciate everything
you're doing for Haruka.

292
00:18:17,996 --> 00:18:18,831
You're welcome.

293
00:18:19,531 --> 00:18:23,202
Do I have to stay in bed
until the surgery?

294
00:18:24,303 --> 00:18:26,472
Walking might aggravate the fracture.

295
00:18:26,772 --> 00:18:28,240
Lessons are out of the question.

296
00:18:28,807 --> 00:18:29,641
Okay.

297
00:18:30,609 --> 00:18:32,678
We thought it was

298
00:18:32,911 --> 00:18:36,648
the end of her dream to
become a ballerina. Right?

299
00:18:38,217 --> 00:18:41,887
Just stay off your feet
until the surgery.

300
00:18:42,788 --> 00:18:43,655
Doctor.

301
00:18:44,857 --> 00:18:47,826
What's your dream, Dr. Daimon?

302
00:18:48,393 --> 00:18:49,228
My dream?

303
00:18:49,795 --> 00:18:52,197
Haruka... Sorry.

304
00:18:52,998 --> 00:18:56,568
Obviously, her dream was
to become a doctor.

305
00:18:57,469 --> 00:19:01,306
So she's someone who
achieved her dream.

306
00:19:02,040 --> 00:19:03,775
Yeah, you're right.

307
00:19:06,545 --> 00:19:07,546
That's not totally true.

308
00:19:09,047 --> 00:19:10,315
My dream is

309
00:19:11,083 --> 00:19:13,819
to keep operating for
as long as possible

310
00:19:14,019 --> 00:19:16,455
and on as many patients
as I can.

311
00:19:20,392 --> 00:19:22,461
Dr. Daimon,
we need to talk.

312
00:19:24,930 --> 00:19:26,298
What's this?

313
00:19:33,972 --> 00:19:34,873
What's going on?!

314
00:19:35,240 --> 00:19:37,409
Why did they all turn us down?!

315
00:19:37,543 --> 00:19:42,447
We received emails from them
almost simultaneously.

316
00:19:42,514 --> 00:19:43,749
I'm asking why.

317
00:19:44,082 --> 00:19:48,153
We called them right away
but they won't tell us why.

318
00:19:48,287 --> 00:19:51,490
They must be wary about
stepping outside their field.

319
00:19:51,557 --> 00:19:54,626
They're not medical engineers after all.

320
00:19:54,693 --> 00:19:56,595
It's no use.
We already tried.

321
00:19:56,662 --> 00:19:58,363
I'll go talk to them.

322
00:20:00,399 --> 00:20:03,035
Notice of business dealing suspension.

323
00:20:11,443 --> 00:20:12,311
Dr. Daimon.

324
00:20:15,447 --> 00:20:16,949
It's no use talking to them.

325
00:20:17,583 --> 00:20:19,184
You never know until you try.

326
00:20:19,751 --> 00:20:21,286
It's pressure from the top.

327
00:20:22,321 --> 00:20:23,188
Pressure?

328
00:20:25,057 --> 00:20:25,991
From who?

329
00:20:30,996 --> 00:20:32,364
Esophagus cancer...

330
00:20:33,131 --> 00:20:34,766
Stage 4A.

331
00:20:36,201 --> 00:20:37,970
I probably only have

332
00:20:38,270 --> 00:20:40,539
about half a year to live.

333
00:20:53,252 --> 00:20:54,620
You can't just barge in.

334
00:20:54,686 --> 00:20:55,887
- Hey!
- Move.

335
00:20:55,954 --> 00:20:58,257
- Wait!
- Hey, you!

336
00:20:58,323 --> 00:20:59,191
You have to leave.

337
00:20:59,258 --> 00:21:01,393
- You!
- That's enough!

338
00:21:01,460 --> 00:21:02,327
It's okay.

339
00:21:14,006 --> 00:21:14,873
Dr. Daimon.

340
00:21:16,875 --> 00:21:18,877
We haven't talked properly.

341
00:21:18,944 --> 00:21:20,078
What are you doing?

342
00:21:21,480 --> 00:21:23,215
You put pressure on them, didn't you?

343
00:21:24,049 --> 00:21:28,320
The people who were willing
to cooperate. Why?

344
00:21:28,854 --> 00:21:29,688
Why?

345
00:21:34,293 --> 00:21:35,227
I heard...

346
00:21:37,195 --> 00:21:38,897
you're Nishiyama's father.

347
00:21:40,599 --> 00:21:43,435
- That's right.
- He's joining the operation.

348
00:21:43,602 --> 00:21:45,470
He's working hard for the patient.

349
00:21:46,838 --> 00:21:48,240
That's the problem.

350
00:21:49,207 --> 00:21:50,409
What do you mean?

351
00:21:50,642 --> 00:21:54,179
You're no good for his future.

352
00:21:57,182 --> 00:22:01,453
I'm hoping that one day
he'll sit in this chair of mine.

353
00:22:03,088 --> 00:22:04,956
That's none of my business.

354
00:22:05,190 --> 00:22:09,094
I want him to walk the royal road
as a doctor.

355
00:22:11,463 --> 00:22:16,435
To properly climb the stairs
of a proper hierarchy.

356
00:22:18,103 --> 00:22:19,104
That is my wish.

357
00:22:21,340 --> 00:22:22,240
So?

358
00:22:23,942 --> 00:22:25,310
I can't tolerate seeing

359
00:22:26,611 --> 00:22:30,482
my son being besmirched
by a lowly freelancer.

360
00:22:33,552 --> 00:22:36,588
I'm terminating the freelancers!

361
00:22:40,258 --> 00:22:41,426
It's still

362
00:22:43,362 --> 00:22:44,563
not too late.

363
00:22:46,531 --> 00:22:47,766
Not too late?

364
00:22:50,335 --> 00:22:52,170
No, it's not too late
for the patient.

365
00:22:53,271 --> 00:22:58,110
Are you going to ruin a patient's
future with your selfishness?!

366
00:22:58,977 --> 00:23:00,545
Dr. Daimon...

367
00:23:01,713 --> 00:23:03,315
I'm looking at the big picture.

368
00:23:05,550 --> 00:23:09,221
Some things can't be overturned
no matter what you say.

369
00:23:11,089 --> 00:23:14,393
It's about time you learn that.

370
00:23:15,927 --> 00:23:17,629
You say you have no restraints

371
00:23:18,463 --> 00:23:20,899
because you're a freelancer

372
00:23:21,433 --> 00:23:25,303
yet you take advantage of
the hospital's advanced equipment

373
00:23:25,637 --> 00:23:27,539
as well as its staff.

374
00:23:28,740 --> 00:23:30,308
You're contradicting yourself.

375
00:23:33,278 --> 00:23:34,346
Isn't that right?

376
00:23:39,251 --> 00:23:43,355
Let's say I have terminal cancer.

377
00:23:44,489 --> 00:23:45,757
What are you talking about?

378
00:23:46,324 --> 00:23:50,762
Even if you were the only
doctor in the world

379
00:23:52,264 --> 00:23:55,867
I wouldn't have an infidel
like you operate on me.

380
00:23:59,171 --> 00:24:03,008
I sit in this chair with such a resolve.

381
00:24:09,648 --> 00:24:12,818
Akira, listen to this.

382
00:24:12,884 --> 00:24:13,785
Hey!

383
00:24:14,853 --> 00:24:15,921
What happened?

384
00:24:17,189 --> 00:24:21,960
The Federation of University Hospitals
is suspending our business dealings.

385
00:24:22,427 --> 00:24:24,062
Suspending business dealings?

386
00:24:27,132 --> 00:24:30,068
And the hospital terminated
your contract.

387
00:24:33,071 --> 00:24:36,575
This is a content-certified
letter from the lawyer.

388
00:24:37,909 --> 00:24:43,482
Kanbara Locum Doctor Agency...
We're getting sued.

389
00:24:43,548 --> 00:24:46,117
Sued for what?

390
00:24:46,585 --> 00:24:49,688
Overcharging clients.
They want refunds.

391
00:24:50,422 --> 00:24:54,326
Our business is suspended
unless they drop the suit.

392
00:24:56,761 --> 00:24:58,296
Is Uchikanda behind this?

393
00:24:58,497 --> 00:24:59,331
I think so.

394
00:25:00,198 --> 00:25:03,401
He can't stand my existence.

395
00:25:03,802 --> 00:25:04,936
Never has.

396
00:25:09,407 --> 00:25:11,076
Akira Kanbara...

397
00:25:13,044 --> 00:25:14,713
You're making a mistake.

398
00:25:15,914 --> 00:25:19,784
Kagenobu Uchikanda,
you're making a mistake.

399
00:25:22,087 --> 00:25:23,121
So what now?

400
00:25:23,755 --> 00:25:27,359
Akira, what are we going to do?

401
00:25:28,426 --> 00:25:29,427
Excuse me.

402
00:25:29,895 --> 00:25:30,795
What do you want?

403
00:25:31,029 --> 00:25:32,731
I was thinking...

404
00:25:32,898 --> 00:25:37,335
If big organizations won't help us,
how about smaller ones?

405
00:25:37,402 --> 00:25:39,137
With the necessary technology.

406
00:25:39,271 --> 00:25:40,505
I know but...

407
00:25:41,873 --> 00:25:46,711
In Japan, rocket parts are made
in small local factories.

408
00:25:49,180 --> 00:25:50,115
Haruka.

409
00:25:50,815 --> 00:25:51,650
This.

410
00:25:51,950 --> 00:25:53,251
Who made it?

411
00:25:54,753 --> 00:25:56,788
KOKONOE PRECISION ENGINEERING

412
00:26:11,469 --> 00:26:12,571
Yes?

413
00:26:14,105 --> 00:26:15,774
I made a rough sketch.

414
00:26:24,482 --> 00:26:26,017
Make this screw from bone?

415
00:26:26,618 --> 00:26:29,254
In the OR during the operation.

416
00:26:29,921 --> 00:26:31,056
In the OR?

417
00:26:31,189 --> 00:26:33,758
I want you to make
the machine in a week.

418
00:26:36,628 --> 00:26:38,196
Can you do it or not?

419
00:27:11,096 --> 00:27:14,132
This workshop has been
closed for almost 10 years.

420
00:27:14,833 --> 00:27:17,002
All the machines are outdated.

421
00:27:18,370 --> 00:27:22,974
Haruka's ballerina key holder
was made here, right?

422
00:27:23,141 --> 00:27:23,975
Yeah.

423
00:27:24,409 --> 00:27:27,212
I made it here.

424
00:27:28,713 --> 00:27:32,250
I was impressed with
all the fine details.

425
00:27:34,185 --> 00:27:35,754
You give me too much credit.

426
00:27:36,721 --> 00:27:39,324
I'm retired and live on pension.

427
00:27:40,592 --> 00:27:41,559
Plus...

428
00:27:44,229 --> 00:27:47,265
metal and bone are completely different.

429
00:27:48,767 --> 00:27:49,768
Fine.

430
00:27:51,736 --> 00:27:55,774
I thought you'd try anything for
your beloved granddaughter.

431
00:27:56,541 --> 00:27:57,709
I was wrong.

432
00:27:59,644 --> 00:28:01,546
I'll find someone else.

433
00:28:05,283 --> 00:28:07,552
When Haruka's mom was in high school

434
00:28:08,753 --> 00:28:11,823
she said she wanted to be a pianist.

435
00:28:12,957 --> 00:28:13,858
But I said no.

436
00:28:14,959 --> 00:28:18,430
I told her she can't feed herself
with the arts.

437
00:28:21,499 --> 00:28:24,669
I crushed my daughter's dream.

438
00:28:25,770 --> 00:28:29,874
When she got pregnant and
wanted to marry the guy

439
00:28:32,377 --> 00:28:33,845
I said no again.

440
00:28:35,013 --> 00:28:36,514
He was a struggling painter.

441
00:28:38,750 --> 00:28:40,085
How can a father
allow that?

442
00:28:40,618 --> 00:28:43,388
I wasn't wrong, was I?

443
00:28:45,457 --> 00:28:46,424
Just as I thought

444
00:28:47,625 --> 00:28:51,362
the guy left her before
Haruka was born.

445
00:28:52,564 --> 00:28:55,133
I'm not interested in
personal stories.

446
00:28:56,568 --> 00:28:58,403
Leave it here.

447
00:29:00,905 --> 00:29:02,707
I didn't say I couldn't do it.

448
00:29:11,216 --> 00:29:16,588
If I can build a machine to
make this screw in a week

449
00:29:17,422 --> 00:29:20,625
Haruka can take the ballet audition?

450
00:29:22,193 --> 00:29:23,027
Yes.

451
00:29:25,029 --> 00:29:27,332
She can keep pursuing her dream?

452
00:29:33,071 --> 00:29:35,507
In any case...

453
00:29:36,207 --> 00:29:38,943
you're bad at drawing.

454
00:29:41,045 --> 00:29:42,413
Sticks and stones.

455
00:29:43,281 --> 00:29:46,818
It's only a matter of time before

456
00:29:46,885 --> 00:29:51,055
Kanbara Locum Doctor Agency
is out of business.

457
00:29:51,389 --> 00:29:54,292
In other words,
Michiko Daimon will be

458
00:29:54,359 --> 00:29:57,228
expelled from Japan's medical community.

459
00:30:00,331 --> 00:30:02,834
Consequently from now on

460
00:30:02,901 --> 00:30:05,937
those who cooperate with her

461
00:30:07,172 --> 00:30:10,175
will be punished accordingly.

462
00:30:11,442 --> 00:30:17,282
My words are those of the chairman
of the Japan Doctors Club.

463
00:30:18,116 --> 00:30:19,617
Understood?

464
00:30:20,451 --> 00:30:21,853
Yes sir. I mean...

465
00:30:22,287 --> 00:30:24,422
Yes, understood clearly.

466
00:30:24,489 --> 00:30:26,925
How about aye-aye-sir?

467
00:31:09,400 --> 00:31:12,337
I was going to leave after two more shots.

468
00:31:14,939 --> 00:31:17,075
I'm a very busy person.

469
00:31:19,944 --> 00:31:20,879
Tequila.

470
00:31:21,079 --> 00:31:22,213
Yes, sir.

471
00:31:23,781 --> 00:31:26,584
Our tastes in liquor haven't changed.

472
00:31:28,553 --> 00:31:30,321
Shall we talk about the good old days?

473
00:31:32,056 --> 00:31:35,059
That's not why I asked you to meet me.

474
00:31:36,761 --> 00:31:41,032
I had heard that your medical
license was revoked.

475
00:31:43,234 --> 00:31:46,905
I thought I'd never see you again.

476
00:31:47,138 --> 00:31:49,274
Unfortunately, here I am.

477
00:31:57,849 --> 00:31:58,716
Another shot.

478
00:31:59,317 --> 00:32:02,320
Why cling to the medical community
that dismissed you?

479
00:32:03,888 --> 00:32:05,089
Why the fixation?

480
00:32:05,490 --> 00:32:06,758
Fixation?

481
00:32:06,858 --> 00:32:08,259
I know the answer.

482
00:32:11,029 --> 00:32:12,397
Michiko Daimon.

483
00:32:14,332 --> 00:32:16,601
How did you mentor her?

484
00:32:21,706 --> 00:32:24,575
I'm not here to talk about the past.

485
00:32:25,376 --> 00:32:26,778
Don't make me repeat myself.

486
00:32:28,212 --> 00:32:34,519
I'm not trying to resist or trample over
your absolute authority.

487
00:32:35,720 --> 00:32:39,590
But I do have one favor to ask.

488
00:32:40,992 --> 00:32:41,960
Favor?

489
00:32:43,394 --> 00:32:45,797
The surgery Michiko plans to do...

490
00:32:47,131 --> 00:32:51,703
Please let her.
Just this one surgery.

491
00:33:06,784 --> 00:33:07,618
Well then...

492
00:33:09,020 --> 00:33:10,989
Is that all you wanted to talk about?

493
00:33:18,830 --> 00:33:22,600
I told you I was leaving
after two shots.

494
00:33:47,558 --> 00:33:49,761
It's getting colder by the day.

495
00:33:51,295 --> 00:33:52,196
Oh...

496
00:33:54,265 --> 00:33:56,934
You shouldn't push yourself too hard.

497
00:33:57,335 --> 00:33:59,137
Right, Ben Casey?

498
00:34:03,307 --> 00:34:04,208
Here.

499
00:34:14,952 --> 00:34:16,320
For a long time

500
00:34:17,054 --> 00:34:21,526
you regretted not being able
to do this in Spain.

501
00:34:30,468 --> 00:34:33,104
Let's go abroad again together

502
00:34:33,438 --> 00:34:36,374
if you can't practice medicine
in Japan anymore.

503
00:34:37,275 --> 00:34:41,245
We'll go where people need us.

504
00:34:42,213 --> 00:34:43,714
Okay, Michiko?

505
00:34:45,583 --> 00:34:47,418
Such a sweet face.

506
00:34:48,152 --> 00:34:50,054
Don't show it to anyone else.

507
00:36:01,159 --> 00:36:02,093
He's late.

508
00:36:02,160 --> 00:36:03,227
I wonder what happened.

509
00:36:03,361 --> 00:36:05,530
Where is he?
Not here yet?

510
00:36:05,596 --> 00:36:07,198
No. I'll call the workshop.

511
00:36:07,265 --> 00:36:08,166
Me too.

512
00:36:08,232 --> 00:36:09,600
We'll see you at the party.

513
00:36:10,835 --> 00:36:13,137
- You know the place?
- Yes.

514
00:36:13,237 --> 00:36:14,739
You're coming later, aren't you?

515
00:36:15,239 --> 00:36:18,209
Dr. Hara has it all set up.
Everyone will be there.

516
00:36:18,843 --> 00:36:23,748
You're official employees of
Totei University Hospital.

517
00:36:24,282 --> 00:36:25,850
Don't forget.

518
00:36:27,618 --> 00:36:29,053
Why is that important?

519
00:36:29,120 --> 00:36:30,922
We'll try to make it.

520
00:36:31,055 --> 00:36:32,223
He's here!

521
00:36:34,091 --> 00:36:35,026
Just in time.

522
00:36:35,126 --> 00:36:36,327
Thank God.

523
00:36:37,895 --> 00:36:39,630
We'll go set it up.

524
00:36:40,298 --> 00:36:41,899
- Don't drop it.
- We won't.

525
00:36:48,105 --> 00:36:49,040
Sorry I'm late.

526
00:36:50,041 --> 00:36:51,475
Let's get ready to roll.

527
00:36:53,444 --> 00:36:54,378
Dr. Ebina.

528
00:36:54,679 --> 00:36:55,513
Yes.

529
00:37:07,892 --> 00:37:11,762
Should we have a metal screw
ready just in case?

530
00:37:12,863 --> 00:37:13,798
Yes, please.

531
00:37:13,864 --> 00:37:14,699
Okay.

532
00:37:32,049 --> 00:37:34,719
Haruka, I'll do my best.

533
00:37:38,322 --> 00:37:40,191
Let's start the anesthesia.

534
00:38:08,619 --> 00:38:11,989
Okay, folks.
Time for the group photo.

535
00:38:12,857 --> 00:38:14,225
Go to that side.

536
00:38:14,292 --> 00:38:17,962
Make sure you're in the camera.

537
00:38:18,029 --> 00:38:20,564
Are you ready?
Here we go.

538
00:38:20,998 --> 00:38:22,466
Okay.

539
00:38:22,566 --> 00:38:26,504
Dr. Inomata, you look too tense.
How about a little smile?

540
00:38:26,570 --> 00:38:28,406
Okay! Here we go.

541
00:38:28,806 --> 00:38:30,541
I want to be in it too.

542
00:38:31,309 --> 00:38:33,377
- Come on.
- Hurry up.

543
00:38:34,011 --> 00:38:36,080
There are so many of us.

544
00:38:36,147 --> 00:38:38,115
There's only that
orthopedic surgery today.

545
00:38:38,182 --> 00:38:39,684
Outside our field.

546
00:38:42,119 --> 00:38:43,254
Until the wee hours...

547
00:38:43,321 --> 00:38:45,289
Yes sir!

548
00:38:48,392 --> 00:38:51,262
I bet you'd rather be
there than here.

549
00:38:51,729 --> 00:38:53,831
I'm the organizer.
Yes, I am.

550
00:38:54,031 --> 00:38:56,667
A role that doesn't require
a medical license.

551
00:38:57,068 --> 00:38:59,337
Don't underestimate
year-end parties.

552
00:38:59,970 --> 00:39:01,138
Cheers!

553
00:39:02,573 --> 00:39:04,108
Did you get the grilled squid?

554
00:39:04,175 --> 00:39:05,343
No? Not yet?

555
00:39:05,409 --> 00:39:06,811
Grilled squid for them.

556
00:39:12,216 --> 00:39:15,986
Be careful not to shake it.
It could shift the home position.

557
00:39:16,187 --> 00:39:17,021
Okay.

558
00:39:25,363 --> 00:39:26,864
For that operation

559
00:39:27,131 --> 00:39:31,302
the patient's grandfather built
a machine to make the screw?

560
00:39:31,402 --> 00:39:32,236
I believe so.

561
00:39:32,370 --> 00:39:35,072
He's just an old guy
from a small workshop.

562
00:39:35,206 --> 00:39:39,443
So how is he going to make
a screw from bone?

563
00:39:39,577 --> 00:39:43,781
If you're so curious,
why aren't you there instead of here?

564
00:39:43,848 --> 00:39:45,249
Yes but... Right?

565
00:39:45,316 --> 00:39:48,619
Being here is better for
future human relations.

566
00:39:48,986 --> 00:39:50,087
You're right.

567
00:39:50,221 --> 00:39:53,290
You're jealous that Nishiyama
is assisting the op.

568
00:39:54,325 --> 00:39:55,826
Not really...

569
00:39:55,926 --> 00:39:57,762
Of course not.

570
00:39:59,296 --> 00:40:04,101
Let's start the osteosynthesis
using autogenous bone graft.

571
00:40:04,435 --> 00:40:05,436
Yes, Doctor.

572
00:40:06,504 --> 00:40:07,571
Good luck.

573
00:40:08,572 --> 00:40:09,907
Good luck to you too.

574
00:40:10,174 --> 00:40:11,075
Scalpel.

575
00:40:17,114 --> 00:40:17,982
Elevator.

576
00:40:32,263 --> 00:40:33,998
Extracting
fragment from ilium.

577
00:40:34,064 --> 00:40:35,166
Micro saw.

578
00:40:50,014 --> 00:40:51,816
First Assistant, secure the field.

579
00:40:51,882 --> 00:40:52,716
Yes, Doctor.

580
00:40:56,187 --> 00:41:00,257
So gentlemen, what are your
plans for the future?

581
00:41:01,459 --> 00:41:03,427
Dr. Hara, another highball.

582
00:41:03,494 --> 00:41:04,395
Another round.

583
00:41:05,396 --> 00:41:09,633
We're slowly but surely
approaching retirement.

584
00:41:09,700 --> 00:41:13,571
Let's not talk about that
right now.

585
00:41:13,637 --> 00:41:18,075
How far up can we go
in the organization?

586
00:41:18,342 --> 00:41:19,810
That's not important.

587
00:41:19,944 --> 00:41:26,217
Enjoy my current position without
clawing desperately up the ladder

588
00:41:26,283 --> 00:41:29,019
and close the curtain with grace.

589
00:41:29,086 --> 00:41:32,923
Those are my themes nowadays.

590
00:41:33,958 --> 00:41:37,661
We've reached the age where

591
00:41:37,728 --> 00:41:41,966
we should embrace
the positions we're in.

592
00:41:42,500 --> 00:41:44,902
Hara, I said another highball.

593
00:41:44,969 --> 00:41:47,071
I don't underestimate it.

594
00:41:47,137 --> 00:41:51,041
Dr. Ebina, I definitely do not
underestimate year-end parties.

595
00:41:51,775 --> 00:41:53,277
Dr. Torii wants another highball.

596
00:41:53,344 --> 00:41:56,113
It's not included in the set menu.

597
00:41:56,180 --> 00:41:57,581
- Not included.
- You never told me.

598
00:41:57,915 --> 00:42:01,318
He didn't read the invitation
I handed out.

599
00:42:02,653 --> 00:42:05,923
That's a weak-ass ambition.

600
00:42:05,990 --> 00:42:07,825
Aim for the top.

601
00:42:07,892 --> 00:42:11,262
Then let me ask you something.

602
00:42:11,328 --> 00:42:15,032
You think you can
move up the ladder?

603
00:42:15,099 --> 00:42:17,001
Life is full of challenges.

604
00:42:17,067 --> 00:42:18,102
Yes!

605
00:42:18,702 --> 00:42:20,037
Changes and challenges!

606
00:42:20,170 --> 00:42:21,906
Challenges!

607
00:42:22,740 --> 00:42:27,278
Can we face the challenges at our age?

608
00:42:27,344 --> 00:42:29,346
That's a good question.

609
00:42:29,413 --> 00:42:32,116
Hey... Ebi... You...

610
00:42:32,349 --> 00:42:34,385
Giving up on becoming
the chief surgeon?

611
00:42:34,518 --> 00:42:35,986
I didn't say that.

612
00:42:36,120 --> 00:42:37,521
Wait a second.

613
00:42:37,655 --> 00:42:40,991
One thing I can say for sure.

614
00:42:41,225 --> 00:42:42,793
You'll never be chief surgeon.

615
00:42:43,894 --> 00:42:45,262
I'll never be chief surgeon.

616
00:42:46,931 --> 00:42:48,799
What'd you just say?!

617
00:43:00,844 --> 00:43:02,813
Extraction complete.
Take it.

618
00:43:02,880 --> 00:43:03,747
Yes, Doctor.

619
00:43:04,415 --> 00:43:06,250
Exposing the
navicular bone.

620
00:43:06,317 --> 00:43:07,585
- Scalpel.
- Yes, Doctor.

621
00:43:19,496 --> 00:43:20,331
Here you go.

622
00:43:36,480 --> 00:43:37,348
Elevator.

623
00:43:42,419 --> 00:43:45,589
I thought Dr. Daimon was
terminated from this hospital.

624
00:43:45,656 --> 00:43:47,791
She was but...

625
00:43:48,192 --> 00:43:51,195
Chairman Uchikanda gave
her the green light.

626
00:43:51,662 --> 00:43:55,432
Just for this one final surgery.

627
00:43:57,334 --> 00:43:58,869
In any case,

628
00:43:59,637 --> 00:44:02,940
this will be Daimon's very last operation.

629
00:44:06,010 --> 00:44:06,977
Daimon...

630
00:44:07,411 --> 00:44:09,880
Opening a hole. Drill.

631
00:44:32,703 --> 00:44:34,405
Damn. It broke.

632
00:44:36,473 --> 00:44:37,841
It broke.

633
00:44:38,042 --> 00:44:41,011
I have to adjust the feed rate.

634
00:44:41,078 --> 00:44:44,314
Let's use the tibia.
The ilium isn't strong enough.

635
00:44:44,381 --> 00:44:45,983
Change the operative field.

636
00:44:46,316 --> 00:44:47,751
Yes, Doctor. Scalpel.

637
00:44:47,918 --> 00:44:48,819
Hurry.

638
00:44:48,919 --> 00:44:49,987
Make it quick.

639
00:44:50,120 --> 00:44:51,555
Let me adjust the machine.

640
00:44:52,056 --> 00:44:54,725
The feed rate and
cutting depth are critical.

641
00:44:54,992 --> 00:44:57,428
Minor adjustments.
It won't take that long.

642
00:44:57,795 --> 00:44:58,662
Can you do it?

643
00:44:59,463 --> 00:45:00,297
Yeah.

644
00:45:12,776 --> 00:45:13,911
Nishiyama.

645
00:45:13,977 --> 00:45:15,345
- Focus.
- Yes, Doctor.

646
00:45:23,554 --> 00:45:25,889
- More drinks.
- We're waiting.

647
00:45:25,956 --> 00:45:27,825
Get us more drinks!

648
00:45:27,891 --> 00:45:28,892
Be quiet.

649
00:45:32,563 --> 00:45:33,397
Damn it.

650
00:45:36,166 --> 00:45:38,135
Dr. Inomata,
can we have a word?

651
00:45:38,202 --> 00:45:40,003
You're an idiot!

652
00:45:40,070 --> 00:45:41,338
Then Dr. Ebina?

653
00:45:41,638 --> 00:45:43,040
You guys drinking?

654
00:45:43,173 --> 00:45:46,610
We want to make sure
if this is the right thing.

655
00:45:46,777 --> 00:45:52,149
Being here and drinking...
We're doing the right thing, aren't we?

656
00:45:52,216 --> 00:45:54,551
Use your brain and
think for yourselves.

657
00:45:54,685 --> 00:45:57,121
I'd also like to know.

658
00:45:57,187 --> 00:45:59,556
What do you want to know?

659
00:45:59,690 --> 00:46:02,292
Should we consider

660
00:46:02,760 --> 00:46:07,131
this year-end party as
a part of our jobs?

661
00:46:07,197 --> 00:46:10,100
Why do you keep asking?

662
00:46:10,234 --> 00:46:12,503
Stop looking to us for answers.

663
00:46:12,636 --> 00:46:15,639
You're not obligated to
attend these parties.

664
00:46:15,773 --> 00:46:17,307
We're not obligated?

665
00:46:17,374 --> 00:46:19,743
But we're being forced to be here.

666
00:46:19,810 --> 00:46:21,278
Nobody forced you.

667
00:46:21,345 --> 00:46:22,412
We're definitely being forced.

668
00:46:22,546 --> 00:46:24,615
You guys, that's enough!

669
00:46:27,718 --> 00:46:29,987
Put yourselves in my shoes.

670
00:46:31,388 --> 00:46:33,657
I'm always stuck in the middle,

671
00:46:34,291 --> 00:46:36,794
trying to make everyone happy.

672
00:46:37,094 --> 00:46:42,299
This isn't why I got a medical license!

673
00:46:43,567 --> 00:46:45,068
Arima. Kurokawa.

674
00:46:45,335 --> 00:46:50,474
These men are bad examples as
doctors, human beings, and men.

675
00:46:50,674 --> 00:46:51,542
Wait.

676
00:46:53,210 --> 00:46:55,412
Did you say as doctors?

677
00:46:55,546 --> 00:46:56,914
As human beings?

678
00:46:57,047 --> 00:46:59,049
And as men?
That comment...

679
00:46:59,183 --> 00:47:00,651
I can't let it slide.

680
00:47:01,285 --> 00:47:03,854
Is that how you see us?

681
00:47:04,121 --> 00:47:07,090
You really think so?

682
00:47:08,025 --> 00:47:09,092
No...

683
00:47:09,159 --> 00:47:13,096
I was a candidate for the Hopkins
Master Medical Research Award.

684
00:47:14,431 --> 00:47:15,265
A bad example?

685
00:47:15,933 --> 00:47:17,768
- No...
- Hey.

686
00:47:19,102 --> 00:47:21,038
Why are we drinking?

687
00:47:21,271 --> 00:47:22,806
Why are we here?

688
00:47:23,140 --> 00:47:25,108
There's no theme.

689
00:47:26,944 --> 00:47:27,945
He's right.

690
00:47:28,779 --> 00:47:32,616
They're working hard in the OR.

691
00:47:37,354 --> 00:47:41,225
I shouldn't be wasting my time
organizing a party.

692
00:47:47,831 --> 00:47:50,300
SURGERY TIME

693
00:47:52,402 --> 00:47:54,004
Extracted. Ready?

694
00:47:55,072 --> 00:47:56,106
How much longer?

695
00:47:58,942 --> 00:48:00,978
This should do it.

696
00:48:01,678 --> 00:48:03,146
- Give me the bone.
- Okay.

697
00:48:08,986 --> 00:48:09,887
Here.

698
00:48:28,605 --> 00:48:30,440
If I pull this off,

699
00:48:30,674 --> 00:48:33,610
will Haruka be able to dance again?

700
00:48:35,445 --> 00:48:37,281
As long as you don't fail.

701
00:48:37,915 --> 00:48:39,416
Because I never do.

702
00:48:57,901 --> 00:48:58,735
There.

703
00:48:59,569 --> 00:49:00,404
It's done.

704
00:49:02,606 --> 00:49:03,440
Take it.

705
00:49:03,807 --> 00:49:04,641
Okay.

706
00:49:05,609 --> 00:49:06,510
Here it is.

707
00:49:07,511 --> 00:49:08,512
Screwdriver.

708
00:49:46,683 --> 00:49:48,185
It's a perfect fit.

709
00:49:48,785 --> 00:49:49,619
Thank you.

710
00:49:51,588 --> 00:49:52,723
Are you okay?

711
00:49:53,390 --> 00:49:54,257
Yes.

712
00:49:55,092 --> 00:49:57,194
Cutting the protrusion.
Micro saw.

713
00:50:04,801 --> 00:50:05,969
Finished.

714
00:50:06,837 --> 00:50:08,271
Good job.

715
00:50:14,878 --> 00:50:17,314
Your grandpa was awesome.

716
00:50:36,266 --> 00:50:39,202
"Haruka, I'm so happy for you."

717
00:50:45,842 --> 00:50:46,676
Doctor...

718
00:50:54,351 --> 00:50:58,088
This is the story of
a lone wolf woman doctor.

719
00:50:59,289 --> 00:51:03,226
This is esophagus cancer.

720
00:51:03,360 --> 00:51:06,163
Stage 4A, perhaps?

721
00:51:06,530 --> 00:51:07,697
Director Hiruma...

722
00:51:09,132 --> 00:51:12,002
Can you cure this patient
here at Totei?

723
00:51:13,437 --> 00:51:14,638
Is it possible?

724
00:51:14,771 --> 00:51:19,910
Even with the expertise of
our hospital... I'm not sure.

725
00:51:20,410 --> 00:51:22,412
Data analysis complete.

726
00:51:22,479 --> 00:51:25,282
Surgery is infeasible.

727
00:51:25,348 --> 00:51:26,183
Okay.

728
00:51:29,853 --> 00:51:33,623
Chairman, if I may be blunt...

729
00:51:35,325 --> 00:51:37,861
it's too late for this patient.

730
00:51:39,296 --> 00:51:42,499
Yes. I agree.

731
00:51:42,833 --> 00:51:48,138
I'm reluctant to accept this patient
at Totei University Hospital.

732
00:51:50,240 --> 00:51:54,044
I believe it would be wise
to turn him away.

733
00:51:55,011 --> 00:51:56,046
I see.

734
00:51:57,247 --> 00:51:58,849
Excuse me.

735
00:51:59,883 --> 00:52:01,284
You're here.

736
00:52:03,153 --> 00:52:08,725
Thank you for employing Daimon
and Jonouchi from our agency.

737
00:52:09,326 --> 00:52:10,327
Melon.

738
00:52:11,895 --> 00:52:13,029
The bill.

739
00:52:13,730 --> 00:52:14,564
Yes.

740
00:52:15,398 --> 00:52:19,336
Ah, the distinguished chairman
of the Japan Doctors Club.

741
00:52:19,669 --> 00:52:22,439
I'm daunted by your presence.

742
00:52:22,672 --> 00:52:25,408
The last time I'll be seeing this bill.

743
00:52:26,343 --> 00:52:30,847
$100,000 isn't too bad if
it'll make you go away for good.

744
00:52:31,681 --> 00:52:35,485
I heard, Mr. Kanbara.

745
00:52:35,986 --> 00:52:39,556
The contract between you
and our hospital...

746
00:52:40,657 --> 00:52:43,026
It's been terminated.

747
00:52:43,426 --> 00:52:44,794
Knock on wood.

748
00:52:45,529 --> 00:52:49,833
I have no choice but
to accept the situation.

749
00:52:52,169 --> 00:52:58,708
Unlike you, we don't cling
to a single institution.

750
00:53:00,343 --> 00:53:04,681
We don't fixate on remaining
in a chair we occupy.

751
00:53:06,550 --> 00:53:09,052
Oh... This...

752
00:53:10,120 --> 00:53:15,025
It appears to be esophagus cancer
in stage 4A.

753
00:53:15,625 --> 00:53:17,527
This tumor can be removed.

754
00:53:18,328 --> 00:53:19,329
Daimon can do it.

755
00:53:22,599 --> 00:53:24,134
Mr. Akira Kanbara.

756
00:53:24,267 --> 00:53:25,135
Yes?

757
00:53:25,202 --> 00:53:32,108
You've been banned from
Totei University Hospital.

758
00:53:32,742 --> 00:53:33,677
Do you understand?

759
00:53:34,544 --> 00:53:37,581
Yes, that's right.
I've been banned.

760
00:53:38,114 --> 00:53:41,318
Well then, I'll say goodbye.

761
00:53:45,755 --> 00:53:46,723
So long.

762
00:53:52,062 --> 00:53:55,265
Let's go! Let's go!

763
00:53:55,999 --> 00:53:57,367
In 2017

764
00:53:57,867 --> 00:54:03,240
the university medical system
regained its once-lost authority

765
00:54:03,707 --> 00:54:09,980
and the system on which lives depend
strayed away from what it should be.

766
00:54:10,046 --> 00:54:14,084
Let's go! Let's go! Aki!

767
00:54:18,622 --> 00:54:19,456
Chairman.

768
00:54:20,824 --> 00:54:22,826
This patient...

769
00:54:25,595 --> 00:54:27,063
Who is it?

770
00:54:45,782 --> 00:54:50,053
TOKYO INTERNATIONAL BALLET AUDITION

771
00:55:27,357 --> 00:55:32,095
In the midst of this, doctors free
from any establishment emerged.

772
00:55:32,195 --> 00:55:36,566
Freelance doctors, in other words,
lone wolf doctors.

773
00:55:37,934 --> 00:55:40,570
The results should be out soon.

774
00:55:41,004 --> 00:55:43,039
Even I'm getting nervous.

775
00:55:43,173 --> 00:55:44,307
Oh, come on.

776
00:55:45,342 --> 00:55:47,010
TOKYO INTERNATIONAL BALLET AUDITION

777
00:55:47,344 --> 00:55:49,346
I can't wait.
There they are.

778
00:55:49,512 --> 00:55:50,747
I was so nervous.

779
00:55:50,880 --> 00:55:53,183
Let's go celebrate.

780
00:56:01,791 --> 00:56:02,659
How did it go?

781
00:56:06,696 --> 00:56:08,832
There were better dancers.

782
00:56:10,967 --> 00:56:11,835
I'm sorry.

783
00:56:13,136 --> 00:56:16,906
Maybe this is a good opportunity
to give up on becoming a ballerina.

784
00:56:20,443 --> 00:56:23,012
You have a long life ahead of you.

785
00:56:23,747 --> 00:56:25,882
Go to high school and college.

786
00:56:26,216 --> 00:56:27,984
You still have a lot of time to think.

787
00:56:31,688 --> 00:56:35,492
Years ago, your grandfather said
the same thing to me.

788
00:56:37,026 --> 00:56:39,429
I couldn't accept it at the time.

789
00:56:40,897 --> 00:56:41,998
But he was right.

790
00:56:43,933 --> 00:56:46,403
He knew what he was talking about.

791
00:56:47,737 --> 00:56:48,605
Hey...

792
00:56:49,506 --> 00:56:53,510
What I said to you that day...
All these years...

793
00:56:54,077 --> 00:56:57,414
I've been regretting it.

794
00:57:04,320 --> 00:57:07,257
I won't quit ballet.

795
00:57:10,727 --> 00:57:15,532
I don't care if I can't be a principal
or if I'm not the best.

796
00:57:16,499 --> 00:57:18,902
I love ballet.

797
00:57:21,271 --> 00:57:22,539
Dr. Daimon.

798
00:57:23,440 --> 00:57:26,576
My dream is to keep dancing

799
00:57:26,676 --> 00:57:30,079
for as long as I can,
as many times as I can.

800
00:57:30,880 --> 00:57:31,714
That's it.

801
00:57:33,249 --> 00:57:35,485
I've heard that line before.

802
00:57:36,453 --> 00:57:38,188
<i>This woman, for example.</i>

803
00:57:39,322 --> 00:57:43,359
<i>Despising the herd mentality, authority</i>
<i>and institutional restraints...</i>

804
00:57:43,760 --> 00:57:48,965
<i>Her solo weapons are her license</i>
<i>and the skills she has acquired.</i>

805
00:57:51,768 --> 00:57:52,635
She's good.

806
00:57:53,236 --> 00:57:54,971
Thank you.

807
00:57:55,205 --> 00:57:56,206
See you.

808
00:57:56,272 --> 00:57:58,541
<i>Surgeon Michiko Daimon.</i>

809
00:57:59,008 --> 00:58:00,043
<i>Also known as...</i>

810
00:58:00,577 --> 00:58:02,345
<i>Doctor-X.</i>

811
00:58:06,115 --> 00:58:07,650
This would be perfect for Mai.

812
00:58:07,717 --> 00:58:09,352
It's too flashy.

813
00:58:09,419 --> 00:58:10,787
You think so?

814
00:58:11,120 --> 00:58:12,322
How about this one?

815
00:58:12,388 --> 00:58:13,456
It's even flashier.

816
00:58:13,523 --> 00:58:15,458
Yeah but it's cute.

817
00:58:17,861 --> 00:58:20,396
Which do you like better?

818
00:58:21,331 --> 00:58:22,332
Boring.

819
00:58:22,665 --> 00:58:24,100
Keep your voice down.

820
00:58:24,634 --> 00:58:25,802
Just say which.

821
00:58:27,270 --> 00:58:29,305
Boring, huh?

822
00:58:29,372 --> 00:58:31,574
But Dr. Daimon likes flashy clothes.

823
00:58:54,264 --> 00:58:55,665
FINAL EPISODE

824
00:58:55,798 --> 00:58:58,001
It's scary being a patient.

825
00:58:58,067 --> 00:59:00,236
I won't let a freelancer
operate on me.

826
00:59:00,370 --> 00:59:04,541
What's most important is to
not back out on the patient.

827
00:59:04,607 --> 00:59:08,578
I want you to stay alive
for much, much longer.
